{
  "formatVersion": 2,
  "title": "Bus voltage failure, lock, and switching delays",
  "description": "Click the PSU label of line 1.2 to cut its bus voltage: the switch actuator switches output L1 off, as set for a bus voltage failure, its card turns grey, and the line coupler no longer forwards telegrams to the line. Click again to restore the voltage: L1 returns to its state before the failure and the actuator sends its status. Input 2 locks L1 (cleaning lock): while locked, L1 stays off and commands are stored. Input 3 switches L2 with a 2-second switch-on delay and a 5-second switch-off delay.",
